meta {
  name: Admin notification sender keys (GET /v1/admin/notifications/sender-keys)
  type: http
  seq: 139
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/admin/notifications/sender-keys
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{adminToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
}

docs {
  # GET /v1/admin/notifications/sender-keys

  The companion app's re-pin surface — the same published set the account surface serves, since
  the sender keys belong to the instance, not to whoever is asking.

  Admin-authed: the master token (shown here) **or** an active device's signed request. Unlike
  registration, reading the set is a plain admin read, so the master token is accepted.

  The pinned set lands in the app's `admin-pairings` keychain document and is refreshed on every
  contact with the relay. See `GET /v1/notifications/sender-keys` for the rotation semantics.

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "keys": [
      { "kid": 3, "publicKey": "did:key:zDnae..." }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - `401` / `403` — missing/invalid admin credential
  - `501` — this instance has no `[notifications] relay` configured
  - `503` — a relay is configured but no signing-key master key is set (see the account-surface
    route's note: an error, deliberately, rather than an empty set)
}
